PART 10 — CHECKOUT AND FINANCIAL INTEGRATION

This is an extremely important section.

The new catalogue must connect to the existing checkout and financial systems.

10.1 Checkout Review

Before checkout, display:

- All selected products.
- Quantities.
- Product prices.
- Item totals.
- Grand total.

Require explicit user confirmation.

10.2 Existing Split Functionality

Preserve the existing feature that allows users to split purchases with named people.

Users should continue to be able to:

- Select a purchase.
- Split the amount.
- Assign portions to named people.
- Track who owes whom.
- Review their outstanding balances.

Do not remove or replace the existing Ledger integration.

If appropriate, allow splitting the entire cart or selected items, while preserving the existing supported split workflow.

10.3 Transaction Integration

After successful checkout:

- Create the appropriate record using the existing transaction system.
- Update the existing budget.
- Update the remaining balance.
- Update the Ledger where applicable.
- Update spending by category.
- Make the purchase available to Audit.
- Make relevant product purchase data available to Price Trend Tracker.
- Update frequently purchased product statistics.

Ensure one checkout does not generate duplicate transactions.

10.4 Checkout Safety

Do not:

- Automatically deduct money merely because a product was added to the cart.
- Create transactions before confirmation.
- Count the same checkout twice.
- Bypass existing split or ledger logic.

Checkout must remain the single point where the purchase becomes a completed financial transaction.

